From: Jake Snyder <jsnyder81@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: WLAN Pi: keep PCIe ASPM disabled on WCN7850

ath12k disables ASPM L0s/L1 on the endpoint for firmware download and,
for chips with hw_params->supports_aspm, restores the saved link-control
value in ath12k_pci_start() once the firmware is up.

On the WLAN Pi M4+ (BCM2711 PCIe bridge) the WCN7850/WCN7851 stops
delivering events to the host as soon as ASPM is restored: the last
event seen is the rfkill state change during init, HTC TX credits are
never returned, every subsequent WMI command hits the 3 s credit
timeout ("wmi command 12291 timeout", "failed to create WMI vdev 0:
-11"), the regulatory domain stays at country 00, scans and monitor
capture return nothing, and unloading the driver hangs the system.
Booting with pcie_aspm=off or pcie_aspm.policy=performance makes the
same kernel/firmware fully functional (73 BSSs across 2.4/5/6 GHz,
monitor capture on all bands, 11d country resolved).

Treat WCN7850 like the QCN9274/IPQ parts and leave the link in L0 after
init. This only touches the endpoint's own link-control register while
ath12k is bound, unlike the global cmdline/Kconfig alternatives.
Power cost is a few hundred mW on an idle link, which a WLAN Pi in
monitor mode never has anyway.

This is a WLAN Pi local patch, not from ath-next.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -516,7 +516,10 @@ static const struct ath12k_hw_params ath12k_hw_params[] = {
 
 		.iova_mask = ATH12K_PCIE_MAX_PAYLOAD_SIZE - 1,
 
-		.supports_aspm = true,
+		/* WLAN Pi: the BCM2711/BCM2712 bridge loses the WCN7850 once
+		 * ASPM is restored after firmware boot; keep the link in L0.
+		 */
+		.supports_aspm = false,
 
 		.ce_ie_addr = NULL,
 		.ce_remap = NULL,
